  "s2_evidence_anchors_A_to_F": [
    [
      "P320",
      "PDF p. 5 / printed p. 201 and PDF p. 7 / printed p. 203.",
      "The AI initiates and guides the analysis, elicits individual contributions, moderates discussion, synthesizes responses, and enriches the output under the prescribed tutor protocol.",
      "PDF pp. 7-11 / printed pp. 203-207.",
      "Observed behavior is compared with the prescribed tutor role and workflow through protocol compliance, adaptability, feedback quality, moderation, personalization, critical depth, and documented deviations.",
      "The evidence comes from four students in one course, one group, and three constrained commercial systems. Ratings were consensus judgments rather than independently validated scale scores; no objective learning-outcome effect or general Alignment instrument was established."
    ],
    [
      "P321",
      "PDF p. 6 / printed p. 8; PDF p. 7 / printed p. 9; PDF p. 9 / printed p. 11.",
      "The proposed assistant can autonomously initiate interaction after errors, inactivity, elapsed time, or performance signals and shift roles across training phases; this behavior is specified but not implemented.",
      "PDF pp. 2-4 and 6-10 / printed pp. 4-6 and 8-12.",
      "The framework maps role, initiative, task allocation, control, transparency, explanation, modality, and adaptive support to trainee expertise, task state, performance, learning goals, expectations, and needs.",
      "The company observation and interview support requirements and design, not validation of the proposed assistant or framework. No completed AI-VR implementation, trainee study, usability result, human-factor result, or longitudinal trust evidence is reported; all planned metrics must remain prospective."
    ],
    [
      "P322",
      "PDF p. 3 / printed p. 2 and PDF pp. 6-7 / printed pp. 5-6.",
      "At review level, systems range to autonomous AI acting independently and AI as teammate, facilitator, mediator, or leader in decision-making, delegation, and conflict-resolution roles.",
      "PDF pp. 5-7 / printed pp. 4-6.",
      "The synthesis connects role clarity, task allocation, AI-task fit, command order, expertise, expectations, autonomy, control, delegation, capability, transparency, and trust dynamics.",
      "Trust is not treated as Alignment by itself. Eligibility and coding are limited to the review's explicit role, task, autonomy, capability, expectation, and control relations. The 22 reviewed studies do not all necessarily satisfy I3, must not be added as clusters through this report, and the proposed framework remains unvalidated."
    ]
  ],
